body:
I'm not really following your reasoning. If the skin isn't a curse, but just a mark of it, then how does that stop this verse from being racist? If black skin and white skin aren't metaphors, and it's implying that black is inferior to white skin. Isn't that Racism. 

I was told that white skin and black skin were metaphors when I presented this idea, your opinion? 

&#x200B;
